<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Solar Flare</h1>
<p>Sphere: Fire Sphere
Class: none (no guild teaches it)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast solar flare &lt;target&gt;
<a cmd='#'>cast solar flare</a>   (at whoever you are fighting)
use a wand or staff of solar flare
</pre>
<p>The caster raises a palm to the sun, shouts 'yarnolf', and the sun itself 
flares down on the target. It is the strongest of the sun spells, and the 
one that depends most on the hour: meant to work only outdoors, in 
daylight, under a clear or cloudy sky, it is fearsome at noon, much weaker 
towards dawn and dusk, and terrible against the undead.
</p><p>It does about as well against any armour, and a shield softens it. Casting 
it is an attack and starts a fight. No guild teaches it, but it turns up on 
wands and staffs among random treasure.
</p><p>Note: at present the spell always fails with "The heavy rain clouds block 
any chance of casting the spell", whatever the weather. This is a known 
bug.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
